  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 317 AM EDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nBy the start of the long term period on Friday, the stage will be \nset for an extended period of drying northwesterly flow at the mid-\nlevels -- with the Southeast situated on the eastern periphery of \nstagnating ridging and within a regime of strong subsidence behind a \ndeepening coastal low across the Eastern Seaboard. An airmass that \noriginated across eastern Canada will be dragged southward on the \nbackside of the aforementioned low, working with the final vestiges \nof a strong CAD event to support more seasonable temperatures for \nlate September: generally in the mid-70s to lower 80s through the \nweekend. Moderation will occur as we move into next week, with \nafternoon highs rising back into the 80s areawide. Morning lows will \nbe crisp and positively fall-like (finally), in the 50s for most. \nContinued subsidence and a comparatively much drier airmass will \nkeep PoPs near-negligible through midweek next week (<15%, which is \nthe delineator between dry and mention of isolated rain chances).",
